! v1.19.0: fills a cell of the capability matrix that no test
! reached.  The Hybrid column had IRC at
! `not run`: B3LYP is the functional class most users actually
! run, and its reaction-path following path was verified nowhere.
!
! This is a TRIPWIRE, not an oracle: the pinned value was recorded
! from this build.  It proves the path keeps producing what it
! produces today, which is what the empty cell was missing.
! Consumes the Hessian written by test_v1190_b3lyp_hcn_tsfreq.
! Declared in the manifest with `needs`, so it runs in that test's
! working directory and is skipped rather than failed if the TS
! search did not converge.
%method B3LYP
%basis sto-3g
%grid 3
%job irc
%read_hess test_v1190_b3lyp_hcn_tsfreq_ts.hess
%irc_step      0.15
%irc_maxpoints 10
%irc_direction both
%charge  0
%mult    1
%hess_method  analytical
%ts_mode 1
%geom_maxiter 80
%geom angstrom
C   -0.55  -0.20   0.00
N    0.55  -0.20   0.00
H    0.00   0.95   0.00
*end
